<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/share> "3" .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Economic Sciences 2001, Joseph E. Stiglitz" .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/year> "2001"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/contribution> "Showed that asymmetric information can provide the key to understanding many observed market phenomena, including unemployment and credit rationing. "@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Award> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/780> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/LaureateAward> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureate/759> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/laureateAward> <http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/793> .
