<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/805> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/year> "2003"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/805> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/contribution> "Developed methods to study the volatility properties of time series in economics, particular in financial markets. His method (ARCH) could, in particular, clarify market developments where turbulent periods, with large fluctuations, are followed by calmer periods, with modest fluctuations."@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/805> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Award> .
