<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/806> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/share> "2" .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/806> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Economic Sciences 2003, Clive W.J. Granger" .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/806> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/year> "2003"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/806> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/contribution> "Developed and applied new statistical methods, based on so-called \"cointegration\", to differentiate between, and combine the analysis of, short-term fluctuations and long-term trends."@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/806> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Award> .
