<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/833> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/contribution> "The first to conduct a full-fledged formal analysis of so-called infinitely repeated games. His research identified exactly what outcomes can be upheld over time in long-run relations (the Folk Theorem)."@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/833> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Award> .
