<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/856> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Economic Sciences 2007, Roger B. Myerson" .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/856> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/year> "2007"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/856> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/contribution> "In the 1970s, the formulation of the \"revelation principle\" (a way of simplifying the search for a feasible mechanism) and implementation theory led to great advances of mechanism design. He developed this principle to perfection and pioneered its application to economic problems such as auctions and regulations."@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/856> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Award> .
