<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/946> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries of machinery regulating vesicle traffic, a major transport system in our cells\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/963> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries of cells that constitute a positioning system in the brain\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/965> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries of cells that constitute a positioning system in the brain\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/964> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries of cells that constitute a positioning system in the brain\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/982> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries concerning a novel therapy against infections caused by roundworm parasites\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/983> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their discoveries concerning a novel therapy against infections caused by roundworm parasites\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/984> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her discoveries concerning a novel therapy against Malaria\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/999> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his discoveries of mechanisms for autophagy\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/999> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans uppt\u00E4ckter av mekanismer f\u00F6r autofagi\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/564> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in special recognition of his poetic composition, which gives evidence of lofty idealism, artistic perfection and a rare combination of the qualities of both heart and intellect\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/564> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som ett erk\u00E4nnande av hans utm\u00E4rkta, j\u00E4mv\u00E4l under senare \u00E5r \u00E5dagalagda f\u00F6rtj\u00E4nster som f\u00F6rfattare och s\u00E4rskilt av hans om h\u00F6g idealitet, konstn\u00E4rlig full\u00E4ndning samt s\u00E4llspord f\u00F6rening av hj\u00E4rtats och snillets egenskaper vittnande diktning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/565> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"the greatest living master of the art of historical writing, with special reference to his monumental work, <I>A history of Rome</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/565> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"nutidens st\u00F6rste levande m\u00E4stare i den historiska framst\u00E4llningens konst, med s\u00E4rskilt f\u00E4st avseende \u00E5 hans monumentala verk R\u00F6mische Geschichte\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/566> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"as a tribute to his noble, magnificent and versatile poetry, which has always been distinguished by both the freshness of its inspiration and the rare purity of its spirit\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/566> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som en g\u00E4rd av erk\u00E4nnande \u00E5t hans \u00E4dla, storartade och m\u00E5ngsidiga skaldeverksamhet, som alltid varit utm\u00E4rkt p\u00E5 en g\u00E5ng av ingivelsens friskhet och av en s\u00E4llsynt sj\u00E4lsrenhet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/567> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of the fresh originality and true inspiration of his poetic production, which faithfully reflects the natural scenery and native spirit of his people, and, in addition, his significant work as a Proven&ccedil;al philologist\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/567> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"med avseende f\u00E4st \u00E5 det ursprungsfriska, snillrika och sant konstn\u00E4rliga i hans diktning, som troget avspeglar hans hembygds natur och folkliv, samt \u00E5 hans betydelsefulla verksamhet som proven&ccedil;alsk filolog\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/568> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of the numerous and brilliant compositions which, in an individual and original manner, have revived the great traditions of the Spanish drama\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/568> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"med avseende f\u00E4st \u00E5 hans omfattande och snillrika f\u00F6rfattarskap, som p\u00E5 sj\u00E4lvst\u00E4ndigt och orginellt s\u00E4tt \u00E5terupplivat det spanska sk\u00E5despelets stora traditioner\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/569> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"because of his outstanding merits as an epic writer\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/569> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"p\u00E5 grund av hans storartade f\u00F6rtj\u00E4nster som episk f\u00F6rfattare\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/570> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"not only in consideration of his deep learning and critical research, but above all as a tribute to the creative energy, freshness of style, and lyrical force which characterize his poetic masterpieces\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/570> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"i betraktande ej blott av hans rika l\u00E4rdom och kritiska forskningar, utan fr\u00E4mst som en hyllning \u00E5t den plastiska energi, den stilens friskhet och den lyriska styrka, som utm\u00E4rka hans poetiska m\u00E4sterverk\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/571> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in consideration of the power of observation, originality of imagination, virility of ideas and remarkable talent for narration which characterize the creations of this world-famous author\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/571> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"i betraktande av den iakttagelsef\u00F6rm\u00E5ga, den ursprungliga inbillningskraft samt den manliga styrka i uppfattning och skildringskonst, som utm\u00E4rka denne v\u00E4rldsber\u00F6mde f\u00F6rfattares skapelser\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/572> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of his earnest search for truth, his penetrating power of thought, his wide range of vision, and the warmth and strength in presentation with which in his numerous works he has vindicated and developed an idealistic philosophy of life\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/572> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"p\u00E5 grund av det sanningss\u00F6kande allvar, den genomtr\u00E4ngande tankekraft och vidsynthet, den v\u00E4rme och styrka i framst\u00E4llningen, varmed han i talrika arbeten h\u00E4vdat och utvecklat en ideal v\u00E4rlds\u00E5sk\u00E5dning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/573> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in appreciation of the lofty idealism, vivid imagination and spiritual perception that characterize her writings\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/573> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"p\u00E5 grund av den \u00E4dla idealitet, den fantasiens rikedom och den framst\u00E4llningens sj\u00E4lfullhet, som pr\u00E4gla hennes diktning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/574> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"as a tribute to the consummate artistry, permeated with idealism, which he has demonstrated during his long productive career as a lyric poet, dramatist, novelist and writer of world-renowned short stories\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/574> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som hyllningsg\u00E4rd \u00E5t den full\u00E4ndade och av ideal uppfattning pr\u00E4glade konstn\u00E4rlighet han \u00E5dagalagt under en l\u00E5ng och betydande verksamhet s\u00E5som lyriker, dramaturg, romanf\u00F6rfattare och diktare av v\u00E4rldsber\u00F6mda noveller\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/575> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in appreciation of his many-sided literary activities, and especially of his dramatic works, which are distinguished by a wealth of imagination and by a poetic fancy, which reveals, sometimes in the guise of a fairy tale, a deep inspiration, while in a mysterious way they appeal to the readers' own feelings and stimulate their imaginations\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/575> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/576> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"primarily in recognition of his fruitful, varied and outstanding production in the realm of dramatic art\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/576> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6rn\u00E4mligast f\u00F6r hans rika, m\u00E5ngsidiga, framst\u00E5ende verksamhet inom den dramatiska diktningens omr\u00E5de\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/577> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"because of his profoundly sensitive, fresh and beautiful verse, by which, with consummate skill, he has made his poetic thought, expressed in his own English words, a part of the literature of the West\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/577> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"p\u00E5 grund av hans dikters djup och h\u00F6ga syftning samt den sk\u00F6nhet och friskhet,som p\u00E5 ett lysande s\u00E4tt inf\u00F6rlivat hans skaldeskap i dess egen engelska dr\u00E4kt \u00E4ven med den v\u00E4sterl\u00E4ndska vitterheten\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/578> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"as a tribute to the lofty idealism of his literary production and to the sympathy and love of truth with which he has described different types of human beings\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/578> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som en hyllning \u00E5t den upph\u00F6jda idealismen i hans f\u00F6rfattarskap samt \u00E5t den medk\u00E4nsla och den sanning med vilka han tecknat olika m\u00E4nniskotyper\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/579> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of his significance as the leading representative of a new era in our literature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/579> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som ett erk\u00E4nnande av hans betydelse som m\u00E5lsmannen f\u00F6r ett nytt skede i v\u00E5r vitterhet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/580> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his varied and rich poetry, which is inspired by lofty ideals\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/580> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans m\u00E5ngsidigt rika och av h\u00F6ga ideal burna diktning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/581> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his authentic descriptions of present-day life in Denmark\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/581> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans full\u00F6diga framst\u00E4llningar av nutida danskt liv\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/582> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in special appreciation of his epic, <I>Olympian Spring</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/582> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"med s\u00E4rskild tanke p\u00E5 hans m\u00E4ktiga epos Olympischer Fr\u00FChling\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/583> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his monumental work, <I>Growth of the Soil</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/583> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans monumentala verk Markens gr\u00F8de\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/584> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of his brilliant literary achievements, characterized as they are by a nobility of style, a profound human sympathy, grace, and a true Gallic temperament\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/584> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"s\u00E5som ett erk\u00E4nnande av hans lysande f\u00F6rfattarverksamhet, pr\u00E4glad av \u00E4del stilkonst, av vidhj\u00E4rtad humanitet, av behag och franskt lynne\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/585> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the happy manner in which he has continued the illustrious traditions of the Spanish drama\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/585> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r det lyckliga s\u00E4tt varp\u00E5 han fullf\u00F6ljt den spanska dramatikens \u00E4rofulla traditioner\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/586> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his always inspired poetry, which in a highly artistic form gives expression to the spirit of a whole nation\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/586> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans st\u00E4ndigt besj\u00E4lade diktning, som i den str\u00E4ngaste konstn\u00E4rliga form ger uttryck \u00E5t ett folks anda\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/587> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his great national epic, <I>The Peasants</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/587> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans stora nationalepos B\u00F6nderna\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/588> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his work which is marked by both idealism and humanity, its stimulating satire often being infused with a singular poetic beauty\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/588> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans av b\u00E5de idealitet och humanitet uppburna f\u00F6rfattarskap, vars friska satir ofta med sig f\u00F6renar en egenartad poetisk sk\u00F6nhet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/589> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her idealistically inspired writings which with plastic clarity picture the life on her native island and with depth and sympathy deal with human problems in general\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/589> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hennes av h\u00F6g idealitet burna f\u00F6rfattarskap, som med plastisk \u00E5sk\u00E5dlighet skildrat livet p\u00E5 hennes f\u00E4derne\u00F6 och med djup och v\u00E4rme behandlat allm\u00E4nt m\u00E4nskliga problem\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/590> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of his rich and vitalizing ideas and the brilliant skill with which they have been presented\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/590> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som ett erk\u00E4nnande \u00E5t hans rika och livgivande id\u00E9er och den gl\u00E4nsande konst varmed de framburits\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/591> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"principally for her powerful descriptions of Northern life during the Middle Ages\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/591> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6rn\u00E4mligast f\u00F6r hennes m\u00E4ktiga skildringar ur Nordens medeltida liv\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/592> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"principally for his great novel, <I>Buddenbrooks</I>, which has won steadily increased recognition as one of the classic works of contemporary literature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/592> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6rn\u00E4mligast f\u00F6r hans stora roman Buddenbrooks, vilken under \u00E5rens lopp vunnit alltmer stadgat erk\u00E4nnande som ett av den samtida litteraturens klassiska verk\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/593> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his vigorous and graphic art of description and his ability to create, with wit and humour, new types of characters\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/593> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans starka och levande skildringskonst, med typskapande f\u00F6rm\u00E5ga, med kvickhet och humor\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/594> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"The poetry of Erik Axel Karlfeldt\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/594> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"Erik Axel Karlfeldts diktning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/595> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his distinguished art of narration which takes its highest form in <I>The Forsyte Saga</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/595> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den f\u00F6rn\u00E4ma skildringskonst, som i The Forsyte Saga uppn\u00E5tt sitt h\u00F6gsta uttryck\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/596> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the strict artistry with which he has carried on the classical Russian traditions in prose writing\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/596> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r det str\u00E4nga konstn\u00E4rskap, varmed han f\u00F6retr\u00E4tt den klassiskt ryska linjen i prosadiktningen\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/597> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his bold and ingenious revival of dramatic and scenic art\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/597> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans dj\u00E4rva och sinnrika nyskapelse av dramats och scenens konst\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/598> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the power, honesty and deep-felt emotions of his dramatic works, which embody an original concept of tragedy\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/598> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans av kraft, \u00E4rlighet och stark k\u00E4nsla samt sj\u00E4lvst\u00E4ndig, tragisk uppfattning pr\u00E4glade dramatik\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/599> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the artistic power and truth with which he has depicted human conflict as well as some fundamental aspects of contemporary life in his novel-cycle <I>Les Thibault</I>\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/599> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den konstn\u00E4rliga kraft och sanning, varmed han i romanserien Les Thibault har framst\u00E4llt m\u00E4nskliga mots\u00E4ttningar och v\u00E4sentliga sidor av samtida liv\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/600> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her rich and truly epic descriptions of peasant life in China and for her biographical masterpieces\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/600> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r rika och \u00E4kta episka skildringar ur kinesiskt bondeliv och f\u00F6r biografiska m\u00E4sterverk\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/601> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his deep understanding of his country's peasantry and the exquisite art with which he has portrayed their way of life and their relationship with Nature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/601> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/602> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the rare strength and fertility of his poetic imagination with which is combined an intellectual curiosity of wide scope and a bold, freshly creative style\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/602> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den s\u00E4llsynta kraften och frodigheten i hans diktarfantasi, f\u00F6renad med vittfamnande intellektualitet och dj\u00E4rv, nyskapande stilkonst\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/603> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her lyric poetry which, inspired by powerful emotions, has made her name a symbol of the idealistic aspirations of the entire Latin American world\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/603> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den av m\u00E4ktig k\u00E4nsla inspirerade lyrik, som gjort hennes diktarnamn till en symbol f\u00F6r hela den latinamerikanska v\u00E4rldens ideella str\u00E4vanden\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/604> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his inspired writings which, while growing in boldness and penetration, exemplify the classical humanitarian ideals and high qualities of style\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/604> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans inspirerade f\u00F6rfattarskap, som i sin utveckling mot dj\u00E4rvhet och djup tillika f\u00F6retr\u00E4der klassiska humanistideal och h\u00F6ga stilv\u00E4rden\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/605> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his comprehensive and artistically significant writings, in which human problems and conditions have been presented with a fearless love of truth and keen psychological insight\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/605> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans vittomfattande och konstn\u00E4rligt betydelsefulla f\u00F6rfattarskap, i vilket m\u00E4nsklighetens fr\u00E5gor och villkor ha framst\u00E4llts med of\u00F6rskr\u00E4ckt sanningsk\u00E4rlek och psykologisk skarpsyn\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/606> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his outstanding, pioneer contribution to present-day poetry\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/606> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans m\u00E4rkliga insats som banbrytare inom nutida poesi\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/607> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his powerful and artistically unique contribution to the modern American novel\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/607> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans kraftfulla och sj\u00E4lvst\u00E4ndigt konstn\u00E4rliga insats i Amerikas nya romanlitteratur\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/608> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of his varied and significant writings in which he champions humanitarian ideals and freedom of thought\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/608> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som ett erk\u00E4nnande \u00E5t hans m\u00E5ngsidiga och betydelsefulla f\u00F6rfattarskap, vari han framtr\u00E4tt som en humanitetens och tankefrihetens f\u00F6rk\u00E4mpe\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/609> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the artistic vigour and true independence of mind with which he endeavours in his poetry to find answers to the eternal questions confronting mankind\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/609> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den konstn\u00E4rliga kraft och djupa sj\u00E4lvst\u00E4ndighet, varmed han i sin diktning s\u00F6ker svar p\u00E5 m\u00E4nniskans eviga fr\u00E5gor\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/610> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the deep spiritual insight and the artistic intensity with which he has in his novels penetrated the drama of human life\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/610> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den genomtr\u00E4ngande sj\u00E4lskunskap och konstn\u00E4rliga intensitet, varmed han i romanens form tolkat det m\u00E4nskliga livsdramat\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/611> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his mastery of historical and biographical description as well as for brilliant oratory in defending exalted human values\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/611> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans m\u00E4sterskap i historisk och biografisk framst\u00E4llning samt f\u00F6r den lysande talekonst, med vilken han framtr\u00E4tt som f\u00F6rsvarare av h\u00F6ga m\u00E4nskliga v\u00E4rden\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/612> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his mastery of the art of narrative, most recently demonstrated in <I>The Old Man and the Sea,</I> and for the influence that he has exerted on contemporary style\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/612> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans kraftfulla och inom nutida ber\u00E4ttarkonst stilbildande m\u00E4sterskap, senast \u00E5dagalagt i The Old Man and the Sea\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/613> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his vivid epic power which has renewed the great narrative art of Iceland\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/613> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans m\u00E5lande epik, som f\u00F6rnyat den stora isl\u00E4ndska ber\u00E4ttarkonsten\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/614> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his lyrical poetry, which in Spanish language constitutes an example of high spirit and artistical purity\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/614> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans lyriska diktning som p\u00E5 spanskt spr\u00E5k bildar ett f\u00F6red\u00F6me av h\u00F6g andlighet och konst\u00E4rlig renhet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/615> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his important literary production, which with clear-sighted earnestness illuminates the problems of the human conscience in our times\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/615> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans betydelsefulla f\u00F6rfattarskap, som med skarpsynt allvar belyser m\u00E4nskliga samvetsproblem i v\u00E5r tid\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/616> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his important achievement both in contemporary lyrical poetry and in the field of the great Russian epic tradition\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/616> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans betydande insats s\u00E5v\u00E4l inom den samtida lyriken som p\u00E5 den stora ryska ber\u00E4ttartraditionens omr\u00E5de\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/617> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his lyrical poetry, which with classical fire expresses the tragic experience of life in our own times\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/617> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans lyriska diktning, som med klassisk eld uttrycker samtidens tragiska livsk\u00E4nsla\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/618> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the soaring flight and the evocative imagery of his poetry which in a visionary fashion reflects the conditions of our time\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/618> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den h\u00F6ga flykten och den bildskapande fantasien i hans diktning, som vision\u00E4rt avspeglar tidsl\u00E4get\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/619> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the epic force with which he has traced themes and depicted human destinies drawn from the history of his country\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/619> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den episka kraft varmed han gestaltat motiv och \u00F6den ur sitt lands historia\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/620> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his realistic and imaginative writings, combining as they do sympathetic humour and keen social perception\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/620> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans p\u00E5 en g\u00E5ng realistiska och fantasifulla ber\u00E4ttarkonst, utm\u00E4rkt av medk\u00E4nnande humor och social skarpsyn\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/621> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his eminent lyrical writing, inspired by a deep feeling for the Hellenic world of culture\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/621> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans framst\u00E5ende lyriska diktning, inspirerad av djup k\u00E4nsla f\u00F6r den hellenska kulturv\u00E4rlden\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/622> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his work which, rich in ideas and filled with the spirit of freedom and the quest for truth, has exerted a far-reaching influence on our age\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/622> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans id\u00E9rika f\u00F6rfattarskap, som genom sin frihetsanda och sanningsstr\u00E4van har ut\u00F6vat ett vidstr\u00E4ckt inflytande i v\u00E5r samtid\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/623> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the artistic power and integrity with which, in his epic of the Don, he has given expression to a historic phase in the life of the Russian people\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/623> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den konstn\u00E4rliga kraft och \u00E4rlighet, varmed han i sitt Donska epos har gestaltat ett historiskt skede i ryska folkets liv\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/624> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his profoundly characteristic narrative art with motifs from the life of the Jewish people\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/624> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans djupt karakt\u00E4rsfulla ber\u00E4ttarkonst med motiv fr\u00E5n det judiska folkets liv\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/625> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her outstanding lyrical and dramatic writing, which interprets Israel's destiny with touching strength\" "@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/625> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hennes framst\u00E5ende lyriska och dramatiska diktning, som med gripande styrka tolkar Israels \u00F6de\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/626> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his vivid literary achievement, deep-rooted in the national traits and traditions of Indian peoples of Latin America\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/626> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans f\u00E4rgstarka diktning med r\u00F6tter i folklig egenart och indianska traditioner\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/627> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his narrative mastery, which with great sensibility expresses the essence of the Japanese mind\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/627> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans ber\u00E4ttarkonst, som med fin k\u00E4nsla uttrycker japanskt v\u00E4sen i dess egenart\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/628> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his writing, which - in new forms for the novel and drama - in the destitution of modern man acquires its elevation\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/628> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en diktning som i nya former f\u00F6r roman och drama ur nutidsm\u00E4nniskans blottst\u00E4lldhet h\u00E4mtar sin konstn\u00E4rliga resning\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/629> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the ethical force with which he has pursued the indispensable traditions of Russian literature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/629> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den etiska kraft varmed han fullf\u00F6ljt den ryska litteraturens omistliga traditioner\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/630> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for a poetry that with the action of an elemental force brings alive a continent's destiny and dreams\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/630> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/631> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his writing which through its combination of a broad perspective on his time and a sensitive skill in characterization has contributed to a renewal of German literature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/631> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en diktning som genom sin f\u00F6rening av tidshistorisk vidsyn och \u00F6msint gestaltningsf\u00F6rm\u00E5ga verkat f\u00F6rnyande inom tysk litteratur\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/632> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for an epic and psychological narrative art which has introduced a new continent into literature\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/632> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en episk och psykologisk ber\u00E4ttarkonst som inf\u00F6rt en ny v\u00E4rldsdel i litteraturen\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/633> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for a narrative art, far-seeing in lands and ages, in the service of freedom\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/633> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en i l\u00E4nder och tider vittsk\u00E5dande ber\u00E4ttarkonst i frihetens tj\u00E4nst\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/634> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for writings that catch the dewdrop and reflect the cosmos\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/634> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r ett f\u00F6rfattarskap som f\u00E5ngar daggdroppen och speglar kosmos\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/635> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his distinctive poetry which, with great artistic sensitivity, has interpreted human values under the sign of an outlook on life with no illusions\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/635> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans s\u00E4rpr\u00E4glade diktning som med stor konstn\u00E4rlig k\u00E4nslighet tolkat humana v\u00E4rden i tecknet av en illusionsfri livssyn\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/636> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the human understanding and subtle analysis of contemporary culture that are combined in his work\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/636> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r den m\u00E4nskliga f\u00F6rst\u00E5else och subtila kulturanalys, som f\u00F6renas i hans verk\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/637> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for a creative poetic writing which illuminates man's condition in the cosmos and in present-day society, at the same time representing the great renewal of the traditions of Spanish poetry between the wars\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/637> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/638> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his impassioned narrative art which, with roots in a Polish-Jewish cultural tradition, brings universal human conditions to life\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/638> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans intensiva ber\u00E4ttarkonst, som med r\u00F6tter i en polsk-judisk kulturtradition levandeg\u00F6r universella m\u00E4nskliga villkor\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/639> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his poetry, which, against the background of Greek tradition, depicts with sensuous strength and intellectual clear-sightedness modern man's struggle for freedom and creativeness\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/639> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/640> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who with uncompromising clear-sightedness voices man's exposed condition in a world of severe conflicts\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/640> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/641> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for writings marked by a broad outlook, a wealth of ideas and artistic power\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/641> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r ett f\u00F6rfattarskap pr\u00E4glat av vid utblick, id\u00E9rikedom och konstn\u00E4rlig kraft\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/642> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his novels and short stories, in which the fantastic and the realistic are combined in a richly composed world of imagination, reflecting a continent's life and conflicts\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/642> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/643> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his novels which, with the perspicuity of realistic narrative art and the diversity and universality of myth, illuminate the human condition in the world of today\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/643> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans romaner som med den realistiska ber\u00E4ttarkonstens \u00E5sk\u00E5dlighet och med mytens m\u00E5ngtydiga allm\u00E4ngiltighet belyser m\u00E4nskliga villkor i dagens v\u00E4rld\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/644> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his poetry which endowed with freshness, sensuality and rich inventiveness provides a liberating image of the indomitable spirit and versatility of man\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/644> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r hans poesi som med frisk sinnlighet och rik uppfinningsf\u00F6rm\u00E5ga ger en befriande bild av m\u00E4nsklig okuvlighet och m\u00E5ngfald\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/645> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in his novel combines the poet's and the painter's creativeness with a deepened awareness of time in the depiction of the human condition\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/645> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/646> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in a wide cultural perspective and with poetic overtones fashions the drama of existence\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/646> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som i ett brett kulturellt perspektiv och med poetiska \u00F6vertoner gestaltar tillvarons drama\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/647> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for an all-embracing authorship, imbued with clarity of thought and poetic intensity\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/647> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r ett vittfamnande f\u00F6rfattarskap, pr\u00E4glat av tankesk\u00E4rpa och poetisk intensitet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/648> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who, through works rich in nuance - now clear-sightedly realistic, now evocatively ambiguous - has formed an Arabian narrative art that applies to all mankind\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/648> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som genom val\u00F6rrika verk - \u00F6msom skarpsynt verklighetsn\u00E4ra, \u00F6msom suggestivt m\u00E5ngtydiga - har format en arabisk romankonst med allm\u00E4nm\u00E4nsklig giltighet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/649> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for a rich and intensive prose, which with restrained compassion forms a challenging vision of man's vulnerability\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/649> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/650> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for impassioned writing with wide horizons, characterized by sensuous intelligence and humanistic integrity\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/650> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en lidelsefull diktning med vida horisonter, pr\u00E4glad av sinnlig intelligens och humanistisk integritet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/651> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who through her magnificent epic writing has - in the words of Alfred Nobel - been of very great benefit to humanity\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/651> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som genom storartad episk diktning har med Alfred Nobels ord - gjort m\u00E4nskligheten den st\u00F6rsta nytta\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/652> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for a poetic oeuvre of great luminosity, sustained by a historical vision, the outcome of a multicultural commitment\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/652> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"f\u00F6r en diktning med stor lyskraft, buren av en historisk vision som vuxit fram ur ett m\u00E5ngkulturellt engagemang\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/653> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in novels characterized by visionary force and poetic import, gives life to an essential aspect of American reality\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/653> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som genom en romankonst pr\u00E4glad av vison\u00E4r kraft och poetisk pregnans levandeg\u00F6r en v\u00E4sentlig sida av amerikansk verklighet\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/654> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who with poetic force creates an imagined world, where life and myth condense to form a disconcerting picture of the human predicament today\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/654> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"som med poetisk kraft skapar en imagin\u00E4r v\u00E4rld, d\u00E4r liv och myt f\u00F6rt\u00E4tas till en skakande bild av m\u00E4nniskans bel\u00E4genhet i nutiden\""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/655> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for works of lyrical beauty and ethical depth, which exalt everyday miracles and the living past\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/655> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/656> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for poetry that with ironic precision allows the historical and biological context to come to light in fragments of human reality\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/656> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/657> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who emulates the jesters of the Middle Ages in scourging authority and upholding the dignity of the downtrodden\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/657> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/658> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who with parables sustained by imagination, compassion and irony continually enables us once again to apprehend an elusory reality\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/658> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/659> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"whose frolicsome black fables portray the forgotten face of history\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/659> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/769> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for an &aelig;uvre of universal validity, bitter insights and linguistic ingenuity, which has opened new paths for the Chinese novel and drama\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/769> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Df\u00F6r ett verk av universell giltighet, bitter insikt och spr\u00E5klig sinnrikhet, som \u00F6ppnat nya v\u00E4gar f\u00F6r kinesisk romankonst och dramatik\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/781> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for having united perceptive narrative and incorruptible scrutiny in works that compel us to see the presence of suppressed histories\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/781> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Df\u00F6r att ha f\u00F6renat lyh\u00F6rt ber\u00E4ttande och omutlig iakttagelse i verk som d\u00F6mer oss att se den borttr\u00E4ngda historiens n\u00E4rvaro\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/795> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for writing that upholds the fragile experience of the individual against the barbaric arbitrariness of history\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/795> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Df\u00F6r ett f\u00F6rfattarskap som h\u00E4vdar den enskildes br\u00E4ckliga erfarenhet mot historiens barbariska godtycke\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/797> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in innumerable guises portrays the surprising involvement of the outsider\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/797> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Dsom i talrika f\u00F6rkl\u00E4dnader framst\u00E4ller utanf\u00F6rskapets\r\n\u00F6verrumplande delaktighet\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/816> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her musical flow of voices and counter-voices in novels and plays that with extraordinary linguistic zeal reveal the absurdity of society's clich&eacute;s and their subjugating power\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/816> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Df\u00F6r hennes musikaliska fl\u00F6de av r\u00F6ster och motr\u00F6ster i\r\nromaner och dramer som med enast\u00E5ende spr\u00E5klig lidelse blottar de sociala klich&eacute;ernas absurditet och tvingande\r\nmakt\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/835> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in his plays uncovers the precipice under everyday prattle and forces entry into oppression's closed rooms\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/842> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who in the quest for the melancholic soul of his native city has discovered new symbols for the clash and interlacing of cultures\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/851> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"that epicist of the female experience, who with scepticism, fire and visionary power has subjected a divided civilisation to scrutiny\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/866> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"author of new departures, poetic adventure and sensual ecstasy, explorer of a humanity beyond and below the reigning civilization\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/878> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who, with the concentration of poetry and the frankness of prose, depicts the landscape of the dispossessed\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/894> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his cartography of structures of power and his trenchant images of the individual's resistance, revolt, and defeat\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/914> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"because, through his condensed, translucent images, he gives us fresh access to reality\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/914> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\u201Df\u00F6r att han i f\u00F6rt\u00E4tade, genomlysta bilder ger oss ny\r\ntillg\u00E5ng till det verkliga\u201D"@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/933> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"who with hallucinatory realism merges folk tales, history and the contemporary\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/952> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"master of the contemporary short story\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/972> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for the art of memory with which he has evoked the most ungraspable human destinies and\r\nuncovered the life-world of the occupation\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/990> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her polyphonic writings, a monument to suffering and courage in our time\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/1009> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for having created new poetic expressions within the great American song tradition\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/544> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his work for peace in Central America, efforts which led to the accord signed in Guatemala on August 7 this year\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/544> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/547> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for his leading role in the peace process which today characterizes important parts of the international community\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/547> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/548> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for her non-violent struggle for democracy and human rights\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/548> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/549> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"in recognition of her work for social justice and ethno-cultural reconciliation based on respect for the rights of indigenous peoples\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/549> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/550> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work for the peaceful termination of the apartheid regime, and for laying the foundations for a new democratic South Africa\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/550> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/551> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work for the peaceful termination of the apartheid regime, and for laying the foundations for a new democratic South Africa\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/551> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/552> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to create peace in the Middle East\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/552> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/553> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to create peace in the Middle East\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/553> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/554> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to create peace in the Middle East\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/554> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/555> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to diminish the part played by nuclear arms in international politics and, in the longer run, to eliminate such arms\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/555> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/556> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to diminish the part played by nuclear arms in international politics and, in the longer run, to eliminate such arms\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/556> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/557> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work towards a just and peaceful solution to the conflict in East Timor\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/557> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/558> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work towards a just and peaceful solution to the conflict in East Timor\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/558> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/559> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work for the banning and clearing of anti-personnel mines\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/559> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/560> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their work for the banning and clearing of anti-personnel mines\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/560> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/561> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to find a peaceful solution to the conflict in Northern Ireland\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/561> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/562> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> "\"for their efforts to find a peaceful solution to the conflict in Northern Ireland\""@en .
<http://data.nobelprize.org/resource/laureateaward/562> <http://data.nobelprize.org/terms/motivation> ""@sv .
